**Cleaning, tested row by row.** The raw trustee files hold {{n_raw_rows}} rows, including {{n_resubmission_duplicates}} resubmitted duplicates, and format B reports its {{n_called_deals_b}} clean-up calls as ordinary repayments. The canonical table rebuilt from those files matches the simulated truth on all {{n_loan_months}} loan-months, with {{canonical_truth_mismatches}} differences.

**Compiler, tested against hand-written SQL.** {{gold_matched}} of {{gold_total}} hand-written queries match the compiler's output, with a worst difference of {{gold_worst_diff}}. All {{oracle_ok}} render to Oracle using only supported constructs.

**Volume.** With the data copied 36 times to {{rows_36x}} loan-months, each of the 34 questions with a numeric answer runs in under {{x36_max_default_s}} seconds with DuckDB's default threads. The slowest single-threaded run takes {{x36_max_single_s}} seconds.

